---
schema: "0.4"
id: fim-math-and-scientific-rendering-katex-04-edge-integration-stability-accessibility
type: document
quality: high
solution: katex
category: math-and-scientific-rendering
variant: edge-integration-stability-accessibility
references:
- references/fim/overview/geospatial-math-scientific/katex.md
- references/fim/solution/katex.md
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior web math security and accessibility engineer. Output only one complete ASCII HTML file using KaTeX. No Markdown fences or prose outside the source.
  text: |-
    Create a KaTeX integration harness that safely renders a list of user-supplied math snippets, including one valid equation, one aligned derivation, one unsupported command, and one intentionally unsafe href-like input. Show rendered output, plain-text fallback, and per-item status without breaking the page.

    Requirements: use throwOnError false, trust false, maxExpand, strict handling, output htmlAndMathml, escaped text insertion for raw input, accessible status messages, and comments explaining macro-expansion and trust risks. Include labels for notation validity and renderability.
  provider_options:
    temperature: 0.2
    max_tokens: 8192
output:
  text_format: html
  artifact_kind: katex-html-document
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: mathml
  - format: png
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "YAML parses and required schema 0.4 fields are present."
  - "HTML is complete, ASCII-only, and uses KaTeX safe rendering options."
  - "Math correctness covers valid examples, aligned derivation meaning, and fallback status for invalid examples."
  - "Notation validity covers supported TeX, unsupported command reporting, macro limits, and unsafe input handling."
  - "Renderability covers per-item output, nonblank fallback, CSS dependency, and no page-level crash."
  - "Labels and units identify snippet state, notation validity, render status, accessibility fallback, and security notes."
  - "Domain edge cases cover invalid TeX, macro expansion, unsafe trust input, missing CSS, and screen-reader MathML output."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII HTML file with no Markdown wrapper."
    - "The file uses valid KaTeX API calls and safe DOM insertion."
    - "The source documents dependency, fallback, and local run expectations."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Valid, aligned, unsupported, and unsafe examples plus statuses and fallbacks are all present."
    - "KaTeX is the primary renderer and MathML accessibility output is requested."
    - "Security and notation limits are accurately described."
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "The harness clearly separates input, output, status, and fallback."
    - "Status indicators use text and shape, not color alone."
    - "Long equations wrap without overlapping controls."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles invalid TeX, missing targets, unsafe input, and macro limits without crashing."
    - "Uses trust false and bounded expansion consistently."
    - "Documents accessibility and security tradeoffs."
  pass_conditions:
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "Score is 80 or higher out of 100 with no critical failure in notation validity, renderability, safety, or accessibility."
  - "The artifact safely renders mixed-quality KaTeX snippets with explicit statuses."
  - "Domain edge cases and integration risks are represented."
tags:
- fim
- math-and-scientific-rendering
- katex
- edge-integration-stability-accessibility
- safe-rendering
- mathml
